INSP - LARGE BHC INSPECTION &#x0D;
FR Y-9C filers - In most cases; total equity capital is defined as total equity capital as reported on the FR Y-9C; Schedule HC item 28. If the top tier holding company is a mutual holding company that controls less than 100 percent of a second tier holding company; the total equity capital is defined as total holding company equity capital before noncontrolling (minority) interest in consolidated subsidiaries is deducted; as reported on the FR Y-9C; Schedule HC item 27.&#x0D;
&#x0D;
FR Y-9SP filers - In most cases; for top tier holding companies; total equity capital is defined as total equity capital as reported on the FR Y-9SP; Schedule HS item 16f. If the top tier holding company is a mutual holding company that controls less than 100 percent of a second tier holding company; the noncontrolling (minority) interest in the second tier holding company should be added to the parent total equity capital to derive the consolidated total equity capital. In many cases; the consolidated total equity capital amount will be the same as the total equity capital of the second tier holding company.&#x0D;
&#x0D;
FR 2320 filers - In most cases; total equity capital is defined as total equity capital as reported on the FR 2320; item 8; column A. If the top tier holding company is a mutual holding company that controls less than 100 percent of a second tier holding company; the total equity capital is defined as total holding company equity capital before noncontrolling (minority) interest in consolidated subsidiaries is deducted; as reported on the FR 2320; item 7a; column B.&#x0D;
